  "explanation": "The original source D1S1 explicitly states that Fort Buchanan was located three miles southwest of present-day Sonoita in Santa Cruz County, Arizona. This provides both the state and more specific geographic context. While D2S1 mentions Nogales, Arizona, in connection with the rediscovery of the ruins, it does not establish Nogales as the location of the fort itself. Therefore, the most accurate and supported answers are Arizona, Santa Cruz County, Arizona, and the precise location near Sonoita."
